{"v":1,"id":["01M7QB5PYSTR804WPDDXMGVD8K","01M7QB5MTF4M0YS3NPTJHX82P1"],"edit.description":{"id":"01M7JHJABPBJR86KWMZW3H95A3","md":"Setup (username, editor, auto sync, emails: this machine) was one chain with init (this repository, pushed to everyone) wedged in the middle, so configuring yourself could stall on, or walk into, initializing a project.\n\n- `epiq setup` runs only the machine questions, then quits: no board, no init offer. Rerunnable; esc quits.\n- `:setup` inside epiq asks the same questions and stays in the TUI.\n- Opening epiq in a git repository without a board offers one (`init` typed, enter or esc). The offer is the screen's: typing `:init` yourself doesn't change the page.\n- `epiq init` starts a board from a script; it needs only an author.\n- init never leaves a repository it then refuses: a failure is taken back, a board on another branch is adopted."}}
