{"v":1,"id":["01M7QBQX5HMY3DS8NHR3E9SSYA","01M7QBQX56J1NE70BZN3W991WR"],"add.issue.comment":{"id":"01M7QBQX5H4QQ2VC80AJX3KVP8","issue":"01M7JHJABPBJR86KWMZW3H95A3","md":"#582: `epiq setup` quits after the machine questions (no init offer); the init screen's offer is its own state, so typing `:init` yourself no longer changes the page.","author":"1K9N43ZQ77QX42RBC9PQ4C9996"}}
{"v":1,"id":["01M7QCC9HFERJFKXWDWGW78H1K","01M7QBQX5HMY3DS8NHR3E9SSYA"],"add.issue":{"id":"01M7QCC9HFM4BJG588EE7NK2MN","parent":"01KVDH0RK4K4MSS29JPPP6WKKC","name":"Setup asks only what it can't guess: no editor question","rank":"7fffffffffffffffffffffff"}}
{"v":1,"id":["01M7QCC9HGY8QSEJZHYC6KF8MS","01M7QCC9HFERJFKXWDWGW78H1K"],"edit.description":{"id":"01M7QCC9HFM4BJG588EE7NK2MN","md":"Onboarding should be a couple of enters. Picking an editor is hard to answer up front, and GUI users never need one.\n\n- Setup no longer asks for an editor. The TUI opens the configured editor, else `$VISUAL`, else `$EDITOR`, else says how to set one (`:config editor <name>`).\n- Auto sync no longer needs an editor configured.\n- `default` / `system` editor suggestions either work or go.\n- The name step is prefilled where it can be (git's `user.name`), so enter is enough."}}
{"v":1,"id":["01M7QDNMNSPAM2G7G0C89P9Z8C","01M7QCC9HGY8QSEJZHYC6KF8MS"],"add.issue.comment":{"id":"01M7QDNMNRDQ2XY73Y4HRKP4K0","issue":"01M7QCC9HFM4BJG588EE7NK2MN","md":"#583: setup is name (git's, prefilled) and auto sync (on); no editor step, the TUI falls back to $VISUAL/$EDITOR and says how to set one. Auto sync and epiq_project_init no longer need an editor; default/system read as unset.","author":"1K9N43ZQ77QX42RBC9PQ4C9996"}}
